What I mean that if this is the case why doesn't MB inform the player 
that a cancellation attack is underway and that it was succesful?

In my opinion the existing message is not properly formed in case of 
resistance.

"The magic-absorbing blade cancels the floating eye!"

This implies that the cancellation has already happened.

Then comes:

"The floating eye resists!"

Which tells that the what actually happened was just a try to cancel the 
monster.

The proper message would be:

"The magic-absorbing blade tries to cancels the floating eye!"

"The floating eye resists!" or "The floating eye is cancelled!"

